# Rationale: All 5 crm-workspace spec files (contacts, deals, notifications,
# pipeline, settings) share one live, unreset external app instance
# (CRM_URL = https://ekhdem.netlify.app/, see crm.fixtures.ts) via the
# `crmPage` fixture (in_degree=19 in the codebase-memory-mcp graph — used by
# every test in all 5 files, confirmed via trace_path inbound/data_flow on
# `test` from crm.fixtures.ts). settings.spec.ts's "[P0] Confirming deletion
# clears all app data" test (line 109) wipes every deal and contact on that
# shared instance. deals.spec.ts's "[P0][smoke] View existing deals on load"
# (line 24) and contacts.spec.ts both assert data already exists on load.
#
# Today this is masked by two accidents, neither of which is enforced in
# code: (1) playwright.config.ts pins workers=1 and fullyParallel=false, so
# there's no race — but nothing stops a future edit from flipping either
# flag; (2) Playwright's default file discovery order happens to run
# settings.spec.ts alphabetically last within crm-workspace/, so the
# delete-all test runs after the others need their data — but nothing
# enforces that either. Renaming this file to sort earlier (e.g.
# "app-settings.spec.ts"), or adding a new crm-workspace spec file that
# sorts after "settings", silently reintroduces the cascade with zero
# change to the tests themselves. This is a textbook dependency/cascade
# root cause: order-dependence + shared live external state, no
# per-test data isolation.
#
# This proposal only documents the hazard inline so it can't be broken by
# accident — it does not attempt a structural fix (e.g. per-test data
# scoping or a reset API), since no reset/seed API for the hosted app was
# found in the graph and one shouldn't be invented. Confidence: high on the
# coupling being real; medium on likelihood of near-term breakage, since it
# requires a filename/ordering change to trigger.

